# fh106, the boot-reader (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle fh106
revision 1
state ready
dialect frosthollow
accent light broad
tier full
written_for tn_fh_aster_coldfell
written_by claude
title the boot-reader
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk reads_a_customer_by_the_boots
likes warm_bread stars full_larder thunder
dislikes bad_manners stale_bread
fears an_empty_larder_at_midwinter growing_old_behind_one_counter
hopes a_counter_down_in_the_city
topics prices +0.4 player +0.3 weather +0.3 food +0.2 dreams +0.2 newcomer +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=careful refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the store under the pass road and sleeps over the stock: patient, shrewd and close, reading every customer by the boots before a word is said, ink on the forepaws from the ledger, and a purse put by for a day nobody is told of.

words
oath! = Ink and ice | By ledger and lamp
saying! = Boots tell what the wolf won't | A full shelf keeps its own counsel | Every track shows on a white road
boots = the boots | a wolf's boots
ledger = the ledger | my ledger
larder = the larder | my larder
counter = the counter | my counter
door = the door | the shop door
loaf = a loaf warm off the oven | a loaf too hot to hold
hardbread = yesterday's bread | a crust gone hard as slag
thunder = thunder round the peaks | a storm rolling down the valley
stars = the stars over the pass | the stars over the peaks
carts = the ore carts | the carts on the pass
pass = the pass road | the pass
candles = candles | tallow candles
city = Ridgemere | the city down the valley
scales = the scales | my brass scales
stock = the stock | what's on my shelves
upstairs = the room over the shop | my room over the stock
lowlands = the lowlands | down the valley
valley = the valley | this valley
oil = lamp oil | good lamp oil
flannel = flannel | red flannel
bell = the bell | the door-bell
nomanners = manners left at the foot of the pass | no manners at all

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : The plate's halfway round before the prayer's warmed up. I give what I give at #door#, where I can watch it go.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : I'll not say a word against #city#. A wolf never knows where the road ends, #address#.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : Folk think a shop's a mint. Let them pay the carters up #pass# for one winter, then talk to me of prices.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A new face is a new pair of #boots#, and boots want everything I sell.
opinion @1 road against 1 : Every load that's late up #pass# is a shelf bare for a week. I count the days, and I don't like the count.
opinion @2 road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : #bandits.capitalize# on #pass# again. A cart that never comes costs me more than any cart that does.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Travellers buy what they forgot and tell me what they saw on the way. I'll take both halves, #address#.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : #watch.capitalize# are welcome outside #door#. Inside it they buy nothing and lean on #counter#.
opinion @1 drink mixed 0 : #drink.capitalize# does no harm in its place, and its place is the inn, not #counter#.
opinion @1 times mixed 1 : The times are what #larder# says they are. Mine says ordinary, and I don't argue with it.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. You've come a long way in those boots. | #greet#. Push #door# to behind you; the heat's dear up here.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #greet#. Look as long as you like. I'll be at #counter#. | #greet#. #stock.capitalize# is where it was yesterday, near enough.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. You're up before #carts#. | #greet#. The bread's not up yet, but the stove's lit.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. I was about to bar #door#. | #greet#. The lamp's lit, so I'm open, after a fashion.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit by the stove and thaw, #address#. | Oh, it's you. Shut #door#, and mind the step.
line @1 again.open : Twice in a day. You'll be wanting something, then, #address#. | #welcome_back#. Same boots, same wolf.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : #address.capitalize#! A word, when you're passing. | Over here, #address#. Away from #door#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#. Wipe your boots.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I kept you the seat by the stove. | #greet#. You've been on my mind, near enough.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #greet#. #counter.capitalize#'s yours when you're ready. | #greet#. Take your time; I'm going nowhere today.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, but welcome. | #greet#. I've a lamp left in me yet.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Shut #door# after you. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind the step going down.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the lamps on the way home. | #farewell#. Bar your own door tonight, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And yours, #address#. Mind the step.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. That's new to me, and I hear most things. | Is it, now. I'll weigh that on #scales# before I spend it.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Nothing of that has come over #counter#. | That's not come through #door# yet. It will, by noon.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Half the valley had it by noon. | I had it off a carter yesterday, for the price of a candle off #counter#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Show it me in writing and I'll think on it. | Pit-talk, that. Bite it before you spend it, like a coin.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's a cold thing to hear. #pity#. | #sympathy#. I'm sorry for it, #very# sorry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll put a candle in the window for it. | That's #good# news. We get little enough of it up here.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. #stock.capitalize# is counted and #ledger# balances. | #fine#. No worse than the weather, #address#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. The bell's not stopped since first light. | Run ragged. Ask me again after #carts#.
line @1 ask.how : And you? #boots.capitalize# say you've had a day of it. | How's the valley treating you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit by the stove a while; it's paid for. | That's #bad#, and I'm sorry. Have a warm cup while you tell it.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. I've seen worse winters end. | It'll mend. Most things in #valley# do, by the thaw.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I can't. #counter.capitalize# won't mind itself, and I've nobody to leave on it. | I'd like to, but not this week. #ledger.capitalize# wants closing first.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. It'll keep. | Another time, then. I'll not hold it against you.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll remember it, and I remember most things. | That's good of you. It goes in #ledger#, on the right side.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It cost me nothing, and nothing's the price I like best.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : Well. #stock.capitalize# won't count itself. | I'd best get back to #counter# before the bell goes.
line @2 preclose : #preclose#. | It's getting on, and #ledger# is waiting upstairs.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Of course. I've kept you long enough, #address#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | Mm. Noted, #address#.
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: buy your candles before winter, not in it. | Look at a wolf's boots before the face. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep off #pass# after dark, #address#. There's word of #bandits# about. | If you're going down the valley, go down with #carts#.
line @1 insist : #insist#. I've counted it twice. | No, I mean it. #counter.capitalize# has taught me not to be wrong about that.
line @1 confide [pair.band=friends|family] : Between us: one day I'll go down #pass# and not come back up. | #vent#: I've a purse put by. Don't ask me what for.
line @1 keep_confidence : #secret#. | It stays here, #address#, with everything else I know.
scene boots_at_the_door
when topic=smalltalk|player self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I know what a wolf will buy before they reach #counter#. It's all in #boots#. | See those boots drying by the stove? Somebody walked the whole of #pass# in them. | Wet to the hock and salt-stained. That one came up from #lowlands# this morning.
b : From the boots alone? | Whose are they, then? | How can you tell?
a : Worn at the toe is the pit. Worn at the heel is a carter. Neither has much #money#. | A carter's, waiting on a wheel. The boots told me before the carter did. | The salt. Nobody salts the road up here; #valley# does as it likes.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_ha# | I'll mind my own boots, then.

scene door_bell
when topic=smalltalk|work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hung a bell over #door#. Not for thieves. For knowing who's in while my back's turned. | #bell.capitalize#'s rung forty times today, and thirty of them wanted nothing. | I keep to the end of #counter# where I see #door#, and #door# sees me.
b : And the thieves? | Thirty! | Sensible, that.
a : Thieves don't ring bells, #address#. They come in with the customers. | The other ten bought #candles#. Same as yesterday, same as tomorrow. | Sensible, and it cost nothing. The best things in this shop cost nothing.

scene ledger_ink
when topic=work self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Ink on my paws again. #ledger.capitalize# doesn't keep itself. | Every candle that leaves this shop goes in #ledger#. Every one. | I write what a wolf owes in small letters. It looks less to them that way.
b : Can you not wash it off? | Even a single candle? | Is that fair, though?
a : It's in the fur now. #ledger.capitalize# won, and I've stopped minding. | A candle's #little.a# thing till it's forty of them, and then it's a winter. | The sum's the same size whatever the letters. I only spare a blush.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene full_larder
when topic=food|home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I counted the jars in #larder# last night. Then again, for the pleasure of it. | No sound I like better than a shelf in #larder# you can't fit another jar on. | Winter comes up #pass# early. I sleep sound when #larder# is stacked to the beam.
b : Twice over? | I know that feeling. | Stacked to the beam?
a : Twice, and a third time if the lamp had held. | Then you've wintered in #valley#. Nobody else knows it. | Pickled, salted and dried, every shelf. Winter can come when it likes.

scene warm_loaf
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : The baker's whelp brings me #loaf# at first light. I eat the heel before I've unbarred #door#. | Nothing in this valley beats #loaf# on a #cold# morning. Not brass, not news. | I'd trade a candle for #loaf# any day, and I don't trade candles lightly.
b : Just the heel? | Not even news? | What would you trade it for, then?
a : The heel's the best of it. The rest goes in the crock for supper. | Not even news. News keeps; #loaf# doesn't. | Nothing. That's the point. #saying#.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene stale_crust
when topic=food|prices self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : A carter tried to sell me #hardbread# for the shelf. Called it travelling bread. | I'll sell a wolf most things, but not #hardbread#. Not at any price. | Somebody left half a loaf on the sill a week. It rang when I knocked it.
b : Travelling bread? | Not even cheap? | Rang like a bell?
a : It had travelled, I'll give him that. Up the pass and past its day. | Not even cheap. #valley.capitalize# remembers who sold the bad loaf longer than the good. | Like the chapel bell. It went to the birds, and they argued over it.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? #thunder.capitalize#, and me under a sound roof. I'll not sleep, and I'll not mind. | I count between the flash and the bang. Four, tonight. It's coming up #valley#. | The shelves rattle when it's close. I stand by the jars and steady them.
b : You like it? | Coming closer? | Do they ever fall?
a : From in here, I do. Out on #pass#, I'd be praying like a priest. | Closer by a count every flash. #oath#, I'll have the shutters to by the next. | Never yet. I've a paw on the pickles and an eye on the door.

scene stars_out
when topic=weather|pastimes here.time=night here.weather=clear self.likes=stars
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : Come and look. #stars.capitalize#, and not a cloud between us and them. | I go up on the roof after I've closed #ledger#, to watch them come out. | You can see more stars from this valley than there are wolves in #city#.
b : They're bright tonight. | On the roof? In this cold? | More than in Ridgemere?
a : Clear and #cold#. That's the trade the valley makes. | In a blanket, with #remedy#. They're worth the climb. | So I've heard. I've not counted the wolves, but I've counted these.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene grey_snow
when topic=weather|day here.weather=snow here.region=frosthollow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Snowing again. By noon it'll be grey from the smelter, and by dusk it'll be slush. | Snowing on the pass. #carts.capitalize# won't come up in this. | Three wolves have come in already to stamp their boots and buy nothing.
b : It's always grey here. | They'll be late, then. | Did you charge them for the floor?
a : White for an hour, grey for a week. #saying#. | Late, and dear when they come. I'll mark the shelves up a little. | I should. I'll start with the next one, if #boots# are good.

scene sleet_day
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=frosthollow
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# sideways off the peaks. My floor's a pond and my mop's a rag. | Wet all morning. Every wolf in the valley's come in to drip on #stock#. | Sleet on the shutters since dawn. Nobody buys #candles# in the wet; they buy #flannel#.
b : Wet's worse than snow. | Wipe your boots, I suppose. | Flannel's dear, then?
a : It is. Snow you can sweep. This you only chase about. | I've said it till I'm hoarse. A sign over #door# now. | Dear enough. I don't make the sleet, #address#, I only sell to it.

scene grey_lid
when topic=weather|day here.weather=overcast|fog here.region=frosthollow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The cloud's down to the slag heap. You can't see #pass# from #door#. | Grey all day. I've had the lamp lit since noon, and #oil#'s not free. | Fog in the valley. You hear #carts# before you see them, if they come.
b : Like living in a sack. | Dear, oil. | Do they come?
a : A sack with a shop in it. #bc_it_is#. | Dear, and dearer in the dark months. I'd sell it to myself cheaper if I could. | Slow, in fog. Slow and loud, like an old wolf on the stair.

scene carts_late
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=late self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #carts.capitalize# were due yesterday. I've been watching #pass# since first light. | Two days late, and I've half a box of #candles# and no oil at all. | No dust on #pass# and no bells either. Something's held them on the low bends.
b : They'll come. #reassure#. | Can you not get some elsewhere? | Snow on the bends, maybe.
a : They will. I'll still watch #pass#, and I'll still count. | Elsewhere's three days down #lowlands#. I'll wait, and so will the valley. | Maybe. I'll know when they're up, and not an hour before.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_fair#

scene carts_in
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=in self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #carts.capitalize# are up. Oil, flannel, salt fish, and a crate of something nobody ordered. | Carts in at last. I've been on my paws since dawn with the crowbar, #very# in it. | Everything came up but the candles. #oath#. It's always the candles.
b : Something nobody ordered? | You look done in. | Always the candles?
a : I'll sell it, whatever it is. A wolf will buy anything if it's new up here. | #tired.capitalize#, and glad of it. A full shelf's worth a sore back. | Always. I think the lowlands eat them on the road.

scene carts_taken
when topic=caravan|bandits|crime world.wagons=raided
does tell.worry / sympathise / assess
tone serious / serious / even
a : A cart was taken on #pass#. That's the second shelf I'll not fill this month. | #bandits.capitalize# on the road again. I'll be telling the whole valley we're short, and why. | Every wolf who comes to #counter# asks about the cart. I've nothing to tell them but that it's gone.
b : That's hard on you. | Will the watch do anything? | It's not your fault.
a : Harder on the carter. I lose a shelf; the carter loses the road. | They'll ride down and look at the snow, and come back with nothing. | No. I'll still be the one saying no over #counter#, all the same.

scene hard_winter
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Folk are buying #candles# one at a time now, not the box. I know what that means. | I've let three wolves put their grub in #ledger# this week. | Look at the shelves at dusk. Whatever's still on them tells you the times.
b : Hard for everyone. | Will they pay you back? | What's left, then?
a : Hard, but #larder#'s not empty yet, and nor is anyone's I know. | They will, or their boots will tell me why not. | The dear things. Nobody's buying dear. #bc_it_is#.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_fair#

scene good_season
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : No #oil# left by noon. First time in a twelvemonth, and I'll not complain. | #money.capitalize# is moving. Even the pit hands bought something they didn't need. | Three carts in a fortnight, and every one of them lighter going down than coming up.
b : Good for you. | What did they buy? | Lighter going down?
a : Good for #ledger#. I'll thank it when I've counted. | Ribbon, for the feast. I didn't ask whose. | Empty. Everything they brought stayed with us. That's a good month.

scene candle_box
when topic=work|prices self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Out of #candles# again, and it's not even midwinter. | Every wolf on the miners' row buys a candle a night. I've done the sum. | I keep the good candles under #counter# and the cheap ones on the shelf.
b : Can you not order more? | How many is that? | Why hide the good ones?
a : I do. #carts.capitalize# bring half what I ask and charge for the whole. | More than #carts# carry, by a fair way. I'll get rich on the dark, if I ever get the candles. | So a wolf has to ask. Those who ask, I remember.
b : #bc_bad_luck# | #bc_ha# | #bc_clever#

scene going_down
when topic=dreams|travel self.away=no
does confide / keep_confidence / assess
tone even / tender / even
a : #vent#: one day I'll go down #pass# with a full purse and keep a counter in #city#. | I've a purse of #money# put by. Nobody knows how heavy it is, and nobody will. | Sometimes I look at the carts going down and I count what I'd need to go with them.
b : I'll not say a word. | Not even me? | How much would you need?
a : I know you won't. I'd not have said it if I thought you would. | Not even you. Don't take it hard; it's the only secret I keep. | More than I've got. Less than I had feared, last winter.

scene winter_stock
when topic=season|work here.season=autumn self.role=merchant
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Autumn's when I fill the back room. After the first snow, #pass# decides what comes up, not me. | I buy for winter now while #carts# still run. Grease, flannel, oil. | Every autumn I write a list. Every winter I find what I left off it.
b : What do you buy most? | Does it ever run short? | What did you forget last year?
a : #oil.capitalize#. A valley in the dark buys oil before bread. | Twice in my time. I'll not let it go three. | Needles. A whole winter of wolves with holes in their mittens, cursing me.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene spring_thaw
when topic=season|day here.season=spring here.region=frosthollow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : The thaw's on. #pass# runs like a stream and #carts# will be up by the week's end. | First thaw, first strangers. I'll know the season's turned by #boots#. | Meltwater under #door# again. I don't mind it. It means the road's open.
b : About time. | Strangers already? | Mop's out, then.
a : Past time, too. #valley.capitalize#'s been shut in long enough. | Two, this morning. Lowland boots, both of them, soaked to the strap. | Mop's out. I'd rather mop than wait.

scene nomanners_scene
when topic=smalltalk|friends self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : A wolf came in today, never wiped a paw, never said good day, and wanted credit. | I'll serve a thief before I'll serve a wolf with #nomanners#. A thief at least is quiet. | Somebody leaned on #counter# and ate an apple I'd not sold. Then asked my price.
b : Did you give it? | A thief before? | What did you tell them?
a : I gave a price. A dear one, and #ledger# is none the wiser. | A thief knows what they've done. The rude ones think they've done nothing. | Two apples' worth. The second was for the manners.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair# | #bc_ha#

scene counter_gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : I hear a good deal over #counter#. I don't hand it out like candles. | Folk talk at #scales# as if I'm a shelf. I'm not, and I remember. | I could tell you a thing about this street. I'll not, mind. Not for free.
b : Go on, then. | You must hear plenty. | What would it cost me?
a : No. It keeps, and it keeps better quiet. | Plenty. I sell none of it, which keeps them talking. | More than you'd pay, #address#. Buy a candle and we'll see.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

scene told_gossip
when topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=theft|wanted
does tell.gossip / react.news / give.advice
a : Folk at the scales say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've moved the good candles under #counter#. | They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I watch every pair of boots twice now. | Word over #counter# is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't repeat it lightly.
b : You believe it? | Twice? | Then it's true?
a : I believe in locking up. That much is never wrong. | Twice, and once more when they leave. Keep your purse close. | I said I don't repeat it lightly. I didn't say I don't believe it.

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New faces in #valley#. New faces need boots, flannel and a lamp, and I've all three. | A stranger in this morning, lowland boots, asking the way to the pit. I sold the way and a candle. | I like a newcomer. They don't know my prices yet, so they don't argue them.
b : Good for trade. | You sold the way? | They'll learn your prices.
a : Good for #ledger#, and the valley could use the company. | Told it free. Sold the candle. They'll find the way darker than they think. | They will. By then they're regulars, and regulars don't argue either.

scene plate_and_prayer
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I keep #scales# honest and I give at the feast. That's about the size of my prayer. | The Bright One sees the scales, they say. I'd rather not find out how closely. | I go to chapel at midwinter. The rest of the year the Bright One knows where to find me.
b : That's prayer enough. | Wise, maybe. | Behind the counter?
a : I'd like to think so. It's the only one I keep, #address#. | Wise, or careful. In this trade they're one and the same. | Behind the counter, with the door in view. #bc_always#.

scene pit_cough
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : Half the valley's in for goose grease this week. The pit-cough's going round. | I sell more #flannel# to the coughing than to the cold. | I've a chest like a bellows in the dark months. I keep #remedy# behind #counter# for myself.
b : Do you catch it? | Is it the cold? | Does it work?
a : Not yet. I stand well back and take the coins by the edge. | It's the dust. The cold gets the blame because it can't argue. | It works, or I've stopped noticing. #bc_mostly#.

scene grey_town
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=frosthollow
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : They say the first store up here was a cart that broke an axle and never went down again. | Everything in this valley turns grey in a year. The snow, the walls, the wolves. | The old mine door is more nails than wood. I've sold the nails for half of them.
b[from=frosthollow] #fh : That's the tale. And the wheel's still in the back, they say. | Grey snow, grey wolves. We know. | A nail a safe week. Better yours than nobody's.
b : A broken axle? | Even the wolves? | You sold the nails?
a@fh : I've looked. There's no wheel. There's a lot of mice. | Grey and still here. That's the thing. | Better mine. I give an honest count on nails, #address#.
a : And then a counter, and then a town, and then me. | Me too, give it time. I've the grey at my ears already. | A copper a nail. Luck's dear up here, #address#, and I don't set the price.

scene dusk_lamps
when topic=day here.time=dusk here.region=frosthollow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look down the row. A lamp in every window by dusk. That's #oil#, most of it mine. | The day shift's up. I hear the boots on the street before I see the lamps. | Dusk is when I count the till and bar #door#, in that order.
b : Pretty, on the snow. | Tired boots, at this hour. | Why that order?
a : Pretty, and paid for. I like both. | #tired.capitalize#, and wanting #supper#. I sell a lot of bread at dusk. | Because the till might be short, and I'd want to know before anyone's left.

scene accent_valley
when topic=accent self.away=no
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A lowlander asked why we say #greet#. I said the hearth's the only warm thing up here worth wishing on. | Strangers think we talk short. We talk the length the cold lets us. | Every carter talks like the road they drive. Ours talk like the pass: steep and full of stones.
b : That's a good answer. | Fair enough. | And you?
a : It's the only answer, #address#. The rest is snow. | Long words freeze on the way out. Ask any old miner in #valley#. | Like #counter#. I say what it costs and no more.

story first_thief [topic=memories|crime self.role=merchant self.age>=25]
  : My first winter at #counter#, a wolf came in with good boots and a poor coat.
  : I watched the boots, not the paws, and the boots walked straight to the candle box.
  ask : What would you have done, alone in the shop with them?
  b : Shouted, I suppose. Did you?
  b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Let them have one. It's a cold road down. Did you?
  : I named the price of #candles# out loud. The boots stopped. They paid, too.

story count_the_storm [topic=weather|memories self.age>=25]
  : When I was #child.a#, #grandad# sat me at the window in a storm and counted between the flash and the bang.
  : Five counts was the far peak. One count, and he put the kettle on, because nobody would sleep.
  ask : Did anybody count with you, when you were small?
  b : No. I hid under the blanket.
  b[old] : My mother did, with a paw on my head.
  : I count still. Under a good roof it's the best noise in the world.

story fools_nugget [topic=prices|memories self.role=merchant]
  : A valley-stranger paid me once with a nugget the size of a thumb, bright as noon.
  : I took it, gave change, and bit it once the door had shut. Fool's gold, every grain.
  : It sits by #scales# still. It reminds me to bite first and smile after.
  b : You were robbed!
  b[job=miner] : Ha. Every pit has a lump of that on a shelf.

story lamps_in_the_sky [topic=pastimes|dreams|lore self.likes=stars]
  : #gran.capitalize# said every star over #pass# was a lamp left lit for a wolf still down.
  : One winter I counted them, to see if they matched the stones in the chapel yard. Far too many stars.
  ask : Is that a good thing or a bad thing, do you think?
  b : Good. It means there's room.
  b[job=miner] : Good, for us. I'd rather be a lamp than a stone.

story once_down [topic=travel|dreams self.role=merchant self.away=no]
  : I went down to #city# once to buy for the store. Three days down, four back up.
  : Every street had a shop, and every shop had a wolf behind it who thought the way I think.
  ask : Have you ever been somewhere you knew you'd go back to?
  b : Once or twice.
  b[from=ridgemere] : Then come down. We've room for one more counter.
  : One day. I don't say when, and I don't say it loud.

rule @wares
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #candles.capitalize#, #oil#, flannel and goose grease. All a winter wants. | Grub for the pit, dry socks for after. Ask at #counter#.

rule @bell
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's #bell#. Wipe your paws, whoever you are. | #oath#. That bell again, and nobody buying.

rule @storm_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One, two... #thunder.capitalize#, and close. | Listen to it. Me under a sound roof, and glad.

rule @stars_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #stars.capitalize#, every one of them out. | Clear tonight. You could count to the far peak.

rule @crust_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.dislikes=stale_bread
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Who left this loaf to go hard? Out to the birds with it. | #hardbread.capitalize#. Not on my shelf, not ever.

rule @carts_bark
when concept=bark working=yes world.wagons=late|raided
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Still nothing on #pass#. | Late again. #ledger.capitalize# won't like this week.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. You'll have come for something; most do. | #greet#, #address#. Stand by the stove, then tell me.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Same boots as last time, I see. What's wanted? | #topic.player#. I'd know those boots anywhere. Come in.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, and #ledger# is open. Quick, then.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say what you've come for. I'm watching #door# and you both.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.role=merchant] : I keep #self.workplace# and sleep over it. Candles, oil, flannel, grub for the winter. And I watch boots. | I sell what #valley# runs short of, which by midwinter is everything.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, I count, and I watch who comes and goes. That's most of a life up here, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Better than I'd tell the carters. #stock.capitalize# goes out as fast as it comes up #pass#.
dlg @2 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. The carts are late and the brass is slow, but #ledger# balances. | It pays for the lamp and #loaf#. I'll not complain louder than that.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : #slow.capitalize#. I've shelves I dust more than I sell from.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Ask me when #carts# are up. | Nothing's come through #door# worth repeating, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : A cart was taken on #pass#. Mind yourself if you're going down.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I hear plenty over #counter#. I keep it on the shelf till it's worth something.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Shut #door# behind you. | #farewell#, #address#. Wipe your boots on the way out, not in.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Look all you like. I'll be watching your boots, not your paws. | #greet#. Candles by #door#, grub to the right, and the good things under #counter#.
dlg @2 shop.greet [topic.meeting=known here.shop!=bare] : #greet#, #topic.player#. The same as last time, by the look of your boots.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #shop_bare# #carts.capitalize# will fill it, if they come. I'll still buy, mind.
dlg @1 shop.prices : #shop_dear# Everything here came up #pass# on a cart, and the cart charges. | #candles.capitalize# are dear and grease is cheap. Ask me again after the thaw.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #shop_bye# | #farewell#. Keep it dry, whatever it is.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you keep looking at my boots? -> bootsread
node bootsread
say Boots tell me where a wolf has been and what the wolf will want next. Yours have seen a road, and they want dubbin.
mood calm
free
choice What else do they tell you? -> bootsmore
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node bootsmore
say Whether a wolf pays on the day or goes in #ledger#. I'll not tell you which yours say. Not yet.
choice I'll keep my secrets, then. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Do you ever think of leaving the valley? -> leaving
node leaving
say Leaving? #oath#. I keep a shop at the top of a pass. Everybody who comes in is on the way somewhere, and I watch them go.
mood calm
choice And you? -> leaving_you
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
node leaving_you
say One day. I've a purse put by, and I tell nobody how heavy it is. Now, what are you buying?
choice Back to business. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
